---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"

const title = "Privacy | Wonder Tinker"
const description = "Privacy posture for the static Wonder Tinker site."
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <main id="main" class="site-shell page-stack">
    <article class="page-layout">
      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Wonder Tinker is a static GitHub Pages site. Google Analytics 4 is installed
          for visitor measurement. No tracking pixel, comments system, account flow,
          payment flow, or newsletter backend is installed.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What the site collects</h2>
        <p>
          This repository does not add application code that collects visitor names,
          email addresses, local storage identifiers, or browser fingerprints.
          Reading a page does not create an account, subscribe the visitor, or send data
          to a project-owned backend. Google Analytics 4 uses cookies for visitor
          measurement; see "Analytics and tracking" below for details.
        </p>
        <p>
          GitHub Pages or a visitor's network provider may keep standard delivery logs
          outside this repository. Wonder Tinker does not control those platform logs
          from site code.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site loads display and reading fonts from Google Fonts
          (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>). Those
          requests are used for typography only; they are not an analytics package,
          comments system, account flow, or project-owned tracking backend.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The site uses <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (gtag.js) to measure visitor
          traffic and traffic sources. The tracking script loads on every page in
          production builds and sends data to Google's servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Data collected:</strong> page URLs visited, referrer / traffic source,
          approximate geographic region (country and city derived from IP address, which
          Google anonymizes at the network edge), device type, browser, and session
          timing. First-party cookies distinguish unique visitors and sessions.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Opt-out:</strong> install the official
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out
          browser add-on</a>, use a browser with built-in tracking protection, or block
          <code>googletagmanager.com</code> and <code>google-analytics.com</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Removal:</strong> replace the Measurement ID in
          <code>src/components/Analytics.astro</code> with the placeholder
          <code>G-XXXXXXXXXX</code> and rebuild the site. The script will not load until
          a real ID is restored.
        </p>
        <p>
          No tracking pixel, tag manager, advertising SDK, or session replay script is
          included.
        </p>

        <h2>Content privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Posts must not publish secrets, API keys, private prompts, credentials, raw
          private logs, or personal data. AI model notes are limited to model name,
          model role, and human review boundary.
        </p>

        <h2>Future custom domain</h2>
        <p>
          A future custom-domain change must configure GitHub Pages DNS, add
          <code>public/CNAME</code>, update Astro <code>site</code> and canonical URL
          assumptions, rebuild the site, and confirm that the analytics configuration
          in <code>src/components/Analytics.astro</code> is intentional and unchanged
          during the domain change.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
